  "response_text": "The stack allocation method we used works by initially setting a maximum amount of stack memory, 0x4000 (or 16 KB), starting at that memory value, and working downwards in memory values. MSP_init_val is an initially large number. By subtracting 0x400 from the address of MSP_inti_val, we can calculate a new address to have PSP_val point to. We need to know the initial location of MSP for this to work since the allocation of PSP_val is dependent on the initial value of MSP.\\n",
